#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Castle Itter: Tyrol, 5 May 1945.  A sample game for the Grognard
engine.

Five days after Hitler's death, in a castle on a crag above the
Brixental, a handful of American tankers, a dozen soldiers of the
Wehrmacht who have gone over to the Austrian resistance, a renegade SS
captain and the French statesmen the castle was a prison for hold the
walls against a hundred and more Waffen-SS, the strangest battle of the
Second World War.  Play either side against the computer, or against a
friend at the same screen.

Run it with ./itter (Python 3 with Tk, nothing else).  The game is
saved to ~/.itter.json.  ./itter --selftest checks the map and plays a
game between two computer players.
"""

